    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 run / 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `membershipNumber` formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nSince the value is fully derivable from the owner's own already-assigned fields \u2014 exactly like the existing `displayName` and `initials` \u2014 I implemented it as a read-only derived response field rather than a stored column or a new pipeline step:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipNumber` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that builds `customerCode + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", registrationDate.getYear() % 100)`, null-guarding both source fields.\n\nBoth response paths that mattered (`RespondWithOwnerCreated` and the `GET /api/owners/{id}` responder) already map through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, so the field appears consistently on create and fetch. No DB column or entity field was needed because the value derives entirely from `customerCode` and `registrationDate`, matching the test's note that it is \"seed-independent... derived from the owner's own fields.\"\n\nThe acceptance test `coreMembershipNumberFormat` and the full suite pass.",
